  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 222, 'Fill one page with a word cloud of everything on your mind, big words for big things.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 223, 'Try a two-minute timer: write until it rings, then stop mid-sentence if you need to.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 224, 'Keep a running list today of moments you felt content, even briefly, and read it over tonight.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 225, 'Paste in a photo, a fortune-cookie slip or a scrap of wrapping paper, and write a line beside it.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 226, 'Press a flower or leaf between two pages and note where you found it.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 227, 'Leave a page for a drawing: sketch the view from your window in simple shapes.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 228, 'Trace your hand on the page and write one thing you''re grateful for on each finger.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 229, 'Draw three boxes like a comic strip and sketch a tiny scene from your day in them.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 230, 'Map your favorite route through your town or neighborhood with a few landmarks.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 231, 'Doodle the weather today in the corner of the page, sun, clouds or rain.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 232, 'Draw a tiny portrait of someone you spent time with today, stick figures welcome.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 233, 'Color in a corner of today''s page with whatever shade matches your mood.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 234, 'Glance back at an older entry and add a sticky note with what you''d tell yourself now.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 235, 'Read three earlier pages in a row and write one sentence about what they have in common.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 236, 'Find an entry where you were worried and note how things turned out.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 237, 'Search earlier pages for a small pleasure you wrote about and plan to enjoy it again.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 238, 'Pick one old line that made you smile and copy it onto today''s page.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 239, 'Notice a pattern across your entries, such as a time of day you feel best, and write it down.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 240, 'Remember that skipping a page is fine, and simply write today''s date and pick up where you are.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 241, 'Treat your journal as a place to be messy: write one page today without fixing a single word.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 242, 'Allow yourself to write the same thing as before if it''s still true; repeating is part of it.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 243, 'Keep it private by finding a drawer or bag pocket where your journal can rest unseen.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 244, 'Let spelling and grammar go today: write fast and leave every mistake right where it lands.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 245, 'Give yourself permission to write only half a page, and notice if that feels like a relief.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 246, 'Should heavy feelings surface while you write, stop, take a breath, and reach out to someone you trust.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 247, 'Close today''s entry with one kind sentence addressed to yourself.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 248, 'Sit on your porch, steps or balcony with a warm drink and write about the evening air.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 249, 'Bring your journal on a weekend outing and write a line at each stop.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 250, 'Write by a lake, river or fountain if you can and describe the water''s movement.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 251, 'Settle into a corner of a bookstore and write about a cover that catches your eye.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 252, 'Find a bench at a museum or gallery and describe one piece in a few lines.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 253, 'During a lunch break outside, write down three things you can see moving.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 254, 'Sitting as a passenger on a long drive, write about the landscape rolling by.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 255, 'On a plane or train, write about where you''re headed and what you hope to find there.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 256, 'Write your page in a hotel room or guest room, describing the bed, the window and the quiet.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 257, 'While waiting at an appointment, write a list of small things you''d like to do this weekend.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 258, 'Back from a trip, write five things you want to remember before they fade.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 259, 'Choose a time that fits you, morning or night, and write it on the inside cover as your journal time.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 260, 'Experiment with a new format: a bulleted list instead of sentences.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 261, 'Write a page as a letter to your journal itself, telling it what you hope to use it for.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 262, 'Make a small index on the first page so you can find favorite entries later.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 263, 'Give each entry a short title today, like a chapter in a book.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 264, 'Write with a colored pen today and see whether it changes your mood on the page.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 265, 'Note how long you''d like your entries to be, a line, a paragraph, a page, and try that today.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 266, 'Keep a tiny pocket notebook with you and fill one page with quick observations.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 267, 'Use the first page of a fresh notebook for a short welcome note to yourself.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 268, 'Store a spare pen in your coat pocket so you''re ready to write anywhere.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 269, 'Pair journaling with something you already do daily, like your evening tea, and try it tonight.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 270, 'Try speaking your entry into a voice memo while you fold laundry or make dinner.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 271, 'Record a short audio entry in a quiet spot outdoors, letting the background sounds stay in.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 272, 'Listen back to an old voice memo entry and write one line about how you sounded.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 273, 'Write the first sentence of your entry as soon as you sit down for breakfast.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 274, 'Spend your first five waking minutes writing before you look at any screen.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 275, 'Write a few lines just after you get home, before you take off your shoes.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 276, 'Jot one line in the afternoon slump and one before bed, then compare the two.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 277, 'Write at the kitchen table while dinner cooks, about anything that comes up.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 278, 'End the evening by listing three things you can let wait until tomorrow.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 279, 'Write a few words just before sleep about one thing you''re looking forward to in the morning.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 280, 'Describe what your shoulders and jaw feel like right now, then let them soften and write again.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 281, 'Notice your breathing for a minute and write three words about it.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 282, 'Write about the most comfortable position your body found today.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 283, 'Note where you feel tired and where you feel strong at this moment.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 284, 'Describe how your feet feel after a long day and where they took you.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 285, 'Recall a time you felt at home in your own body and write down where you were.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 286, 'List three movements you enjoyed today, like stretching, dancing or a long walk.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 287, 'Name the emotion closest to the surface right now and where you feel it in your body.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 288, 'Write about a moment today when you felt your heart lift, even a little.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 289, 'Write a short page about what a calm version of today would have looked like.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 290, 'Describe the moment you were most present today.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 291, 'List three things you saw today that were beautiful in an ordinary way.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 292, 'Write about a texture you touched today, rough, soft or smooth, and what it was.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 293, 'As spring arrives, list the first signs of it you''ve spotted and where you saw each one.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 294, 'Plant an idea on the page: one thing you''d like to grow this spring, in your garden or your life.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 295, 'Describe a spring rain, real or remembered, and the smell of wet ground after it.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 296, 'Sketch out, in words, a long summer evening with nowhere to be.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 297, 'List summer foods you love and a memory tied to one of them.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 298, 'Describe the heat of a summer day using three senses besides sight.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 299, 'Write about the first cool morning of fall and how it changes your mood.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 300, 'Collect a fallen leaf on your walk, tape it in, and write where it came from.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 301, 'List what you''d like to put away and what you''d like to take up as the days get shorter.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 302, 'Write about a warm drink you love in winter and the moment you most enjoy it.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 303, 'Describe the first snow you remember, or a winter day where you live now.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 304, 'Write about how you''d like to spend the darkest evenings of the year.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 305, 'Note one holiday memory that still makes you smile, whatever the celebration was.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 306, 'Write about who you''d like to spend the coming holidays with and one thing you''d like to do together.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 307, 'List a few gentle ways to care for yourself during a busy holiday season.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 308, 'Write about a holiday that feels complicated for you, only as much as feels right today.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 309, 'Describe a birthday you remember well, yours or someone else''s.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 310, 'Jot down things you''ve learned since your last birthday, big or small.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 311, 'Write a birthday wish for someone close to you, even if their birthday is months away.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 312, 'Look ahead to the new year and write three small things you''d like to try, not resolutions.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 313, 'Write about the year that''s ending: one high point, one low point and one surprise.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 314, 'Note a hope for the coming year written in the present tense, as if it''s already true.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 315, 'Reflect on the change of seasons by writing what you''d like to leave behind and what you''d like to bring.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 316, 'Write about a season of your life that felt like a turning point.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 317, 'Mark the first day of a new season in your journal with a short note about where you are.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 318, 'Read over your entries from the last season and choose one word that sums it up.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 319, 'Return to the first page you ever wrote here and note one way you''ve changed since.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 320, 'Flip to the pages you enjoyed writing most and note what they share.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 321, 'Compare an early entry with a recent one and write what feels different in your voice.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 322, 'Choose an earlier entry with a worry in it and add a sentence about how you see it now.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 323, 'Select one entry to keep forever and fold down its corner.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 324, 'Pick out a recurring person in your pages and write why they matter to you.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 325, 'Search your journal for a question you asked yourself and try answering it today.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 326, 'Revisit a list you made earlier and add three new items to it.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 327, 'Gather three favorite lines from earlier pages and write them together on one page.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 328, 'Circle every mention of something you enjoyed in your recent entries, then pick one to do again soon.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 329, 'Underline any line in recent pages that sounds like your own best advice.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 330, 'Ask yourself what you would like more of in your entries and try it today.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 331, 'Wonder on paper: what would you explore if you had a whole free week?'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 332, 'Write down a question about the natural world you''ve always wanted answered.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 333, 'Ask a question about someone you love that you''d like to know the answer to.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 334, 'Brainstorm ten questions you''d like to ask yourself in your journal later.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 335, 'Pose one question to yourself tonight and sleep on it before you answer.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 336, 'Speculate on a small mystery from your life, like why a song always moves you.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 337, 'Wonder about a stranger you passed today and write a short imagined story about their day.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 338, 'Imagine meeting yourself in ten years and write the first thing you''d ask.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 339, 'Picture a door in your home opening onto any place in the world, and describe where it leads.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 340, 'Invent a tiny holiday just for you and describe how you''d celebrate it.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 341, 'Dream up a perfect small day using only places within a short walk of home.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 342, 'Plan a pretend trip on paper: the destination, the bag you''d pack, the first meal.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 343, 'Compose a six-word story about your day.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 344, 'Craft a short poem of three lines about something you saw today, no rhyming needed.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 345, 'Turn one ordinary moment from today into the opening line of a novel.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 346, 'Write a short dialogue between two parts of you that want different things today.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 347, 'Create an acrostic using the letters of your name, one word or phrase per line.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 348, 'Fill a page with things you love that begin with the same letter.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 349, 'Describe your day as a weather report: sunny spells, passing clouds, a breeze in the afternoon.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 350, 'Summarize your day as a headline, then write a short subhead beneath it.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 351, 'Describe your day as if it were a recipe, with ingredients and steps.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 352, 'Make a playlist of five songs for today and write one line about why each fits.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 353, 'Write a brief review of your weekend as if it were a favorite restaurant.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 354, 'Compose a thank-you letter to a place that has been good to you.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 355, 'Address a letter you won''t send to someone who hurt you, writing only what you want to say.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 356, 'Pen a letter you won''t send to someone you miss, telling them about your day.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 357, 'Draft a note to a future you who will read this page on a hard day.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 358, 'Write a letter to your journal at the end of a notebook, thanking it for holding your thoughts.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 359, 'Finish a notebook and start the next one with a list of what you hope to fill it with.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 360, 'Celebrate a filled notebook by writing a short table of contents on its last page.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 361, 'Store your finished journals somewhere safe and write a line about where you keep them.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 362, 'Hold your journal for a moment without writing, then jot down how it feels to have this habit.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 363, 'Note what keeps you coming back to the page and write it in one sentence.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 364, 'Reflect on the habit itself: what''s the easiest time, spot and pen for you, and what you''d change.'),
  ('keeping-a-simple-journal', 365, 'Close your journal today by writing one line you''d like to read on the next page you open.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 1, 'Make brief eye contact with one person you pass today and give a small nod.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 2, 'Smile at the next cashier who rings you up, even if you say nothing else.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 3, 'Say "good morning" to one person you pass on your way somewhere before noon.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 4, 'Nod and say "hi" to someone walking a dog on your street or path.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 5, 'Thank a cashier by the name on their name tag, then let them get on with their line.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 6, 'Notice three people today who seem open to a greeting, and smile at just one of them.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 7, 'Hold a door for someone and add "have a good one" as they go through.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 8, 'Wave back at a child who waves at you from a stroller or a car window, with their grown-up in view.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 9, 'Answer "have a nice day" from a worker with a real smile and "thanks, you too."'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 10, 'Greet the bus or shuttle driver with a quick hello as you board.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 11, 'Look up from your phone while you wait in a line today and take in the faces around you.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 12, 'Murmur a warm "excuse me" and a smile when you squeeze past someone in a store aisle.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 13, 'Practice a friendly greeting out loud at home three times, so it feels familiar when you use it.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 14, 'Return a smile from a stranger instead of looking away, even for half a second.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 15, 'Offer a quiet "hello" to someone who passes your table while you sit outside a cafe.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 16, 'Tell the person who bags your groceries "thank you, I appreciate it."'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 17, 'Greet a fellow walker on a trail or park path with "morning" or "evening."'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 18, 'Choose one phrase to keep handy today, such as "Hi, how''s it going?", and use it once.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 19, 'Wish the security guard or front desk worker a good night as you leave a building after dark.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 20, 'Wave and smile at a driver who stops to let you cross the street.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 21, 'Let someone with only a few items go ahead of you in line, and say "go ahead, no rush."'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 22, 'Catch the eye of the server who refills your water and say "thanks."'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 23, 'Greet the person who sits beside you on a bench with a simple "hi," then let the silence be easy.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 24, 'Ask the barista how their morning is going, and listen to the answer before you look at your phone.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 25, 'Notice when someone has headphones in or is rushing, and let them be; save your hello for someone who seems at ease.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 26, 'Offer "bless you" to a stranger who sneezes nearby, with a small smile.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 27, 'Wish the cashier "a good rest of your shift" as you pick up your bag.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 28, 'Greet a mail carrier you pass on the sidewalk with a quick "hi, thanks for all you do."'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 29, 'Smile and nod at another parent or caregiver waiting at a crosswalk or a school pickup line.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 30, 'Call out "nice day for it" to someone else who is out jogging, gardening or washing a car.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 31, 'Comment on the weather to the person beside you at a crosswalk: "Finally some sun, huh?"'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 32, 'Thank the person who holds an elevator for you with a smile and a quick "appreciate it."'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 33, 'Ask "Which floor?" when you step into an elevator first, and press the button for them.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 34, 'Wish a cashier or clerk a happy weekend on a Friday afternoon.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 35, 'Remind yourself before you go out that a short, slightly awkward hello is perfectly normal, then try one.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 36, 'Lift a hand to a farmer on a tractor or a neighbor on a porch as you pass along a quiet country road.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 37, 'Tell a server "that was delicious, thank you" when they clear your plate.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 38, 'Greet the librarian at the desk on your way in, not just on your way out.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 39, 'Reply to a cashier''s "how are you?" with a real answer, like "pretty good, actually," and ask it back.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 40, 'Give a worker handling a long line an encouraging smile as you reach the front, without slowing them down.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 41, 'Thank the pharmacy clerk by name if their tag shows it, and wish them a good evening.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 42, 'Offer a soft "morning" to the person waiting at the bus stop with you, and leave it there if they look busy.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 43, 'Type a friendly "hi everyone" in the chat of a public online class, event or livestream you join.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 44, 'Thank the person cleaning a restroom or lobby as you pass them.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 45, 'Tell a delivery driver "thanks, stay warm" or "thanks, stay cool," whatever the weather calls for.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 46, 'Laugh along when someone near you laughs at something funny you both just saw.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 47, 'Let your face soften as you walk into a store, and see whether anyone smiles back.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 48, 'Pick the staffed checkout lane instead of self-checkout once today, just for the chance to say hello.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 49, 'Greet the person behind the deli or bakery counter before you place your order.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 50, 'Tell someone "thanks for waiting" when they pause so you can go first through a doorway.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 51, 'Wish a gas station clerk a safe night when you pay inside.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 52, 'Nod hello to the regulars at a gym, pool or park you visit, even without speaking.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 53, 'If a greeting falls flat today, let it go, tell yourself "that was fine," and carry on.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 54, 'Pick a smaller step on a low-energy day: one smile at one person is enough.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 55, 'Check with a dog''s owner, "Is it okay to say hi?", before you pet a dog that comes over to sniff you.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 56, 'Thank a crossing guard on your walk with a wave and "thanks for keeping us safe."'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 57, 'Hand a dropped glove, receipt or pen back to a stranger with "I think this is yours."'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 58, 'Wish someone "good luck" if you overhear they''re heading to an interview or an exam and the moment feels natural.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 59, 'Tell the person at a farm stand "these look great" as you pay.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 60, 'Wish a ticket taker "enjoy the show" or "have a good game" when they scan your ticket.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 61, 'Make a point of thanking a toll worker, parking attendant or ferry hand today.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 62, 'Greet the person checking IDs at a door with a friendly hello instead of silence.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 63, 'Wish a worker "enjoy the season" during a busy winter shopping trip, whatever holidays they keep.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 64, 'Notice your shoulders and breath before you greet someone, let them drop, then say hello.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 65, 'Thank a stranger who gives you directions with a full "thank you so much, that really helps."'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 66, 'Greet the attendant at the self-checkout area by name or with a "hi" when they come over to help.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 67, 'Try a friendly "good afternoon" instead of your usual "hi" with one worker today.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 68, 'Smile at a fellow shopper when you both reach for the same item, and say "you go ahead."'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 69, 'Hold the door at a bakery or ice cream shop and tell the person leaving "enjoy!"'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 70, 'Practice ending a tiny exchange kindly: "Nice talking with you, have a good one."'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 71, 'Look back over the greetings you have tried so far in this challenge and pick the one that felt easiest to repeat.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 72, 'Use the name of the next person who introduces themselves to you, once, before you say goodbye.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 73, 'Step outside at sunrise or dusk and say hello to the first person you see out walking.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 74, 'Compliment a dog you meet on a walk, "What a happy dog, what''s their name?", and say the name back.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 75, 'Tell someone working in their front yard that their flowers brighten up your walk.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 76, 'Praise a stranger''s choice of jacket, scarf or hat with "Great color," and keep walking.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 77, 'Admire a bike at a rack while its owner unlocks it: "That''s a beautiful bike, is it good on hills?"'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 78, 'Notice a clever sign or window display and tell the shop worker you liked it.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 79, 'Tell a street musician which song you loved, and drop something in the case if you can.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 80, 'Ask a cashier "Has it been busy today?" and let the answer be as short as they want.'),
  ('starting-conversations-with-strangers', 81, 'Mention to a parent at the playground that their kid''s sandcastle is impressive, then go back to your bench.'),
